WEBVTT

02:00.871 --> 02:03.707
What is your pleasure, Mr. Cotton?

02:04.833 --> 02:07.294
The box.

02:17.638 --> 02:19.974
Take it, it's yours.

02:25.563 --> 02:27.439
It always was.

05:55.523 --> 05:58.484
- It's got to be one of these.
- I'm freezing.

05:58.484 --> 06:01.820
- OK, OK.
- Maybe the lock's been changed.

06:01.820 --> 06:04.782
Like who?
Who's gonna change this lock?

06:04.782 --> 06:08.160
- It was just a suggestion.
- Ah!

06:08.160 --> 06:10.371
Success.

06:10.371 --> 06:12.331
Voilà.

06:12.331 --> 06:14.875
Well, this is it.

06:16.585 --> 06:18.754
The old homestead.

06:24.009 --> 06:26.679
Ugh.

06:26.679 --> 06:29.723
- Smells damp.
- Well, it's, er...

06:29.723 --> 06:32.184
been empty for a while, hasn't it?

06:33.269 --> 06:37.314
But we'll soon warm it up
and get it feeling like a home.

06:38.691 --> 06:42.486
- How long since you were here?
- The better pan of ten years.

06:42.486 --> 06:45.239
I wanted to sell it after the old lady died

06:45.239 --> 06:49.994
but I couldn't get Frank to agree -
I guess he needed a hide-out or something.

06:53.372 --> 06:55.416
Would you look at this?

06:55.416 --> 06:57.585
Don't worry...

06:58.669 --> 07:01.463
this stuff means nothing to me.

07:01.463 --> 07:04.800
- It all goes.
- I thought half of it was your brother's?

07:04.800 --> 07:09.221
I've never known him
to kick cash out of bed, besides...

07:09.221 --> 07:11.724
he's probably behind bars some place.

07:11.724 --> 07:14.518
You know...

07:15.603 --> 07:19.273
We have to let Kirsty see this place
before we do a thing to it.

07:19.398 --> 07:22.193
- She'll love it.
- You really want to move in?

07:23.235 --> 07:26.488
- You don't like it?
- I suppose it's better than Brooklyn.

07:26.488 --> 07:28.574
Oh, don't start, Julia.

07:29.658 --> 07:31.660
- Don't start what?
- Look...

07:31.660 --> 07:34.580
We can make it work here.

07:34.580 --> 07:38.500
I've got a terrific job,
you're back on your own tun'.

07:40.586 --> 07:43.255
- We can be happy.
- All right, all right.

07:43.255 --> 07:45.382
So what's the argument?

07:45.382 --> 07:48.177
- No argument.
- Oh, Christ.

07:48.177 --> 07:50.429
Honey...

07:53.474 --> 07:54.808
Shit.

08:34.556 --> 08:36.976
- Larry!
- Where are you?

08:36.976 --> 08:38.978
In here.

08:46.986 --> 08:48.821
Squatters?

08:53.075 --> 08:55.452
Frank.

08:55.452 --> 08:58.038
- He's here?
- Oh, he's been here.

08:58.038 --> 09:01.292
There's stuff in the kitchen
you wouldn't believe.

09:01.292 --> 09:04.003
He's obviously made
one of his famous getaways.

09:04.003 --> 09:06.672
What the hell's that?

09:23.814 --> 09:26.066
- Who is this?
- 'Dad.'

09:26.192 --> 09:28.569
- Kirsty!
- I got through.

09:28.569 --> 09:31.113
- Barely, where are you?
- I found a room.

09:31.113 --> 09:34.200
- 'What?'
- I said I found a room.

09:34.200 --> 09:37.203
- I thought you were going to stay with us.
- 'Dad?'

09:37.203 --> 09:38.621
'You'd like this house.'

09:38.621 --> 09:40.915
You'd like my room.

09:58.307 --> 10:00.434
I'd really like you to see this house.

10:00.434 --> 10:03.145
Maybe soon, I've got to find myself a job.

10:03.145 --> 10:07.816
What for, sweetie? You've already
made the gesture, there's no need...

10:07.816 --> 10:11.028
This isn't a gesture,
this is something I need to do.

10:12.363 --> 10:14.323
Trust me a little, OK?

10:31.048 --> 10:33.008
Call me tomorrow.

10:33.008 --> 10:35.678
I will. I'll see you.

10:35.678 --> 10:37.137
Bye, Dad.

11:00.160 --> 11:02.496
So?

11:03.455 --> 11:05.666
Why not?

11:05.791 --> 11:07.751
Great.

11:07.751 --> 11:09.795
We'll move in on Sunday.

11:09.795 --> 11:12.882
Look out for the molding...

11:25.644 --> 11:27.897
Don't worry, it'll get through.

11:27.897 --> 11:30.733
- All right. Put it there.
- Oh! You've got my arm!

11:35.905 --> 11:37.740
Let's take five, guys.

11:40.618 --> 11:44.163
- How's things in there?
- Looks like a bomb dropped.

11:44.163 --> 11:46.498
You got any beer?

11:46.498 --> 11:48.584
There's some in the fridge.

11:50.211 --> 11:51.587
Oh, well...

11:51.712 --> 11:53.672
Why don't I get it?

11:55.716 --> 11:57.968
I've got nothing better to do.

13:05.744 --> 13:07.496
Excuse me.

13:07.496 --> 13:10.249
- My lucky day.
- Hi.

13:10.249 --> 13:13.627
- Do you wanna buy a bed?
- Not much.

13:13.752 --> 13:15.296
- Dad!
- Kirsty!

13:15.296 --> 13:18.048
- Hi!
- Hello, sweetie. Come here.

13:18.966 --> 13:21.135
- Here you go.
- Oh, great.

13:21.135 --> 13:23.095
- This is a big house.
- You like?

13:23.095 --> 13:26.140
Yeah. Me like.

13:26.140 --> 13:30.394
I'll give you the grand tour
if we ever get this goddamn bed moved.

13:30.394 --> 13:32.438
- Is Julia here?
- She's upstairs.

13:32.438 --> 13:34.940
Look, be gentle with her, OK?

13:34.940 --> 13:38.277
- She hates moving.
- Surprise.

13:38.277 --> 13:41.155
- Kirsty...
- OK. All right. I'll be nice.

13:41.155 --> 13:44.825
You get on with the grunt work,
I'll make some coffee.

13:44.825 --> 13:47.703
- Great idea, there's the kitchen.
- OK.

13:47.703 --> 13:49.538
Bye.

13:52.249 --> 13:54.418
- That your daughter?
- Uh-huh.

13:54.418 --> 13:57.755
- Got her mother's looks.
- Her mother's dead.

13:57.755 --> 13:59.381
Oh.

14:07.473 --> 14:09.225
Come on!

14:13.646 --> 14:15.314
Oh, shit!

14:17.525 --> 14:19.944
Can I come in'?

14:21.362 --> 14:23.447
Can I come in'?

14:28.619 --> 14:31.163
You're Julia, right?

14:31.163 --> 14:33.457
That's right.

14:33.457 --> 14:36.085
Who are you?

14:36.085 --> 14:37.753
I'm Frank.

14:39.505 --> 14:42.174
I'm brother Frank.

14:42.174 --> 14:44.635
Oh, yes.

14:44.635 --> 14:47.179
I, er... I came for the wedding.

14:50.599 --> 14:52.935
Well, can I come in or not?

14:52.935 --> 14:55.187
I'm sorry. Of course.

14:59.275 --> 15:03.153
- You're very welcome.
- Yeah. That's nice to know.

15:07.032 --> 15:10.744
- Do you have a towel?
- Have you got a towel?

15:10.744 --> 15:12.204
Kirsty.

15:13.455 --> 15:15.749
There's one in the bathroom.

15:17.209 --> 15:19.795
By the way,
did Daddy tell you I got a room?

15:19.795 --> 15:22.464
It's not that big but it's OK.

15:22.464 --> 15:24.508
Julia?

15:27.344 --> 15:30.139
Julia?

16:17.394 --> 16:20.064
'What shall we drink to?'

16:22.858 --> 16:25.069
Wedded bliss?

16:25.861 --> 16:28.447
- I'm very happy.
- Oh, sure you are.

16:31.075 --> 16:33.494
'You gonna let me kiss the bride?'

16:48.759 --> 16:51.971
What about Larry?

16:58.018 --> 16:59.979
Forget him.

18:01.415 --> 18:04.376
Take the weight from me. My foot's stuck.

18:04.376 --> 18:06.003
- You got it?
- I got it.

18:06.003 --> 18:08.422
Now just... push it to me as I pull.

18:35.616 --> 18:37.785
It's never enough.

18:40.704 --> 18:43.666
Julia...

18:48.379 --> 18:50.339
Please?

18:54.718 --> 18:57.096
L-I'll do anything you want.

18:59.598 --> 19:01.183
Anything.

19:13.028 --> 19:14.864
Here.

19:15.948 --> 19:19.326
- Is it deep?
- I don't know, I haven't looked.

19:19.326 --> 19:21.620
You know me and blood.

19:21.620 --> 19:24.498
- I'm gonna faint.
- You're not going to faint.

19:24.498 --> 19:27.418
- Shit.
- L-Let me see.

19:27.418 --> 19:32.298
- Shit.
- Oh, it's going to need stitches.

19:32.298 --> 19:35.718
- I'm going to throw up.
- You're not.

19:35.718 --> 19:39.597
Just take it easy, take it easy.
It's going to be all right.

19:39.597 --> 19:43.767
Let's get you to the hospital.

20:04.622 --> 20:07.875
- What happened?
- It's just an accident, he's all right.

20:07.875 --> 20:10.211
Will you drive? He needs stitches.

20:10.211 --> 20:13.172
- Yeah, sure.
- The keys are in the kitchen.

20:14.256 --> 20:17.218
- So stupid.
- It's all right.

22:43.906 --> 22:47.451
No, I'm not kidding!

22:47.451 --> 22:52.081
The doctor's poking around
with all the delicacy of Josef Mengele

22:52.081 --> 22:53.874
and I worry I'm gonna pass out.

22:53.874 --> 22:55.918
He says, "Of course you're not, old boy."

22:55.918 --> 23:01.173
Next thing I'm on the floor and he's standing
there like he's the one that needs help.

23:01.173 --> 23:04.218
- He was afraid you'd sue him.
- I should do it!

23:04.218 --> 23:07.680
Bill, you know all about that stuff.
We'll sue his ass.

23:14.645 --> 23:17.481
- Doctors!
- That's right, honey.

23:17.481 --> 23:21.318
- What's my darling drinking?
- I don't remember.

23:21.443 --> 23:25.781
- Julia, you want some of this?
- Oh, no more for me, thanks.

23:25.781 --> 23:29.577
OK. OK, stop, I'm not going
to be able to stand up.

23:29.577 --> 23:32.121
So lie down.

23:38.377 --> 23:42.006
Would you all excuse me?
I think I'm going to go to bed.

23:42.006 --> 23:44.675
- Are you all right, darling?
- Uh-huh.

23:44.675 --> 23:47.469
Er, I think we ought
to be making a move too.

23:47.595 --> 23:50.556
No, Bill! Absolutely not!

23:50.556 --> 23:55.060
This is the night of the paper hat here.
We're celebrating... something.

23:55.060 --> 23:57.354
So sit down!

23:57.354 --> 23:59.982
Good night. You have to come to us next.

23:59.982 --> 24:02.943
- Real soon.
- I'm glad you're back.

24:02.943 --> 24:05.029
Thank you. Good night.

24:22.421 --> 24:25.174
- Does it still hurt?
- What?

24:25.174 --> 24:27.384
Oh...

24:27.384 --> 24:29.220
Only when I drink.

25:44.128 --> 25:47.089
Oh... God.

25:59.977 --> 26:02.062
Julia?

26:05.274 --> 26:07.943
Oh, my God.

26:07.943 --> 26:10.529
Don't look at me.

26:13.741 --> 26:16.160
Oh, God... Oh...

26:16.160 --> 26:21.081
- Who are you?
- I said... don't look.

26:23.918 --> 26:25.794
Help me!

26:28.839 --> 26:32.635
Tell me... who you are.

26:34.762 --> 26:36.722
Frank.

26:40.893 --> 26:42.853
No.

26:42.853 --> 26:45.523
- No!
- Believe me.

26:45.523 --> 26:48.442
It's me. It's really me.

26:50.402 --> 26:53.948
His blood... on the floor
- it brought me back.

26:56.742 --> 26:58.744
Back?

27:00.538 --> 27:02.915
F-From where?

27:02.915 --> 27:05.417
Just help me, will you?

27:06.585 --> 27:08.420
Please, God, help me?

27:35.114 --> 27:37.658
- Somebody...
- Wait.

27:52.590 --> 27:55.467
You can't leave me like this, you can't.

27:58.012 --> 28:00.139
What do you want me to do?

28:00.139 --> 28:03.184
The blood brought me this far...

28:03.184 --> 28:04.852
I need more.

28:07.980 --> 28:10.107
You have to heal me!

28:23.162 --> 28:24.663
Hi.

28:25.706 --> 28:27.458
Are you all right?

28:31.086 --> 28:35.674
- Kirsty? I thought I'd lost you.
- No, I'm here.

28:36.967 --> 28:38.928
Good night.

28:59.573 --> 29:03.035
Why didn't you stay at Larry's house?
There's plenty of room.

29:03.160 --> 29:05.746
Yeah, there's room... and there's Julia.

29:05.746 --> 29:07.957
Ah, I see.

29:18.384 --> 29:20.678
She's like you, so damn polite.

29:20.678 --> 29:23.556
- Oh, yeah? Meaning what?
- I don't know, she's...

29:23.556 --> 29:26.475
- She's uptight and frigid.
- I beg your pardon?

29:26.475 --> 29:29.812
There you go. "I beg your pardon?"

29:29.812 --> 29:32.064
- Hey, we're not all frigid.
- Oh, no?

29:32.064 --> 29:34.733
- Oh, no.
- Oh, no?

29:35.693 --> 29:38.487
- Oh, no.
- That's not what I heard.

29:38.487 --> 29:42.116
You must have been speaking
to all the wrong people.

30:21.363 --> 30:23.115
Anything?

30:24.158 --> 30:26.160
Anything.

30:49.642 --> 30:52.394
You'll do it?

30:52.394 --> 30:54.480
Yes.

30:55.523 --> 30:57.358
I Will.

32:08.179 --> 32:10.556
Kirsty? Kirsty?

32:10.556 --> 32:12.600
Kirsty?

32:14.226 --> 32:16.395
- Are you all right?
- Yeah.

32:16.395 --> 32:18.814
I don't know, I...

32:19.857 --> 32:21.859
I- I was dreaming.

32:24.653 --> 32:26.530
Daddy...

32:38.417 --> 32:40.377
Hello?

32:49.970 --> 32:53.891
- I'm all right, honey.
- I wanted to make sure you were OK.

32:54.975 --> 32:58.103
Never better. Now, you sleep well, OK?

32:58.103 --> 33:00.189
'Yeah.'

33:00.314 --> 33:03.150
- I love you, sweetie.
- 'I love you too, Daddy.'

33:03.275 --> 33:05.236
Bye.

33:10.407 --> 33:13.202
- Who was it?
- She had a bad dream.

33:13.202 --> 33:15.579
- Who?
- Kirsty.

33:24.088 --> 33:26.048
Kirsty.

33:53.117 --> 33:55.077
Not much fun, is it?

33:55.077 --> 33:58.122
- What?
- Drinking alone.

34:01.625 --> 34:03.586
Not much.

34:05.504 --> 34:09.800
I thought maybe, er... Well...

34:10.843 --> 34:14.930
if we're both on our own
maybe we could have a drink together.

34:20.685 --> 34:22.062
Why not?

34:28.359 --> 34:31.280
You know, it's not often that I, er...

34:31.280 --> 34:33.948
Well, you know.

34:34.073 --> 34:37.995
- There's a first time for everything.
- That's right, yeah.

34:37.995 --> 34:39.997
I suppose that's right.

34:43.792 --> 34:46.337
Would you, er... like a drink?

34:46.337 --> 34:50.256
Oh, no, no, I'm... well over my limit.

34:53.344 --> 34:56.597
You know, it's funny, but, er...

34:56.597 --> 35:01.519
I... I feel like I've known you for years.

35:01.519 --> 35:03.854
You know?

35:08.567 --> 35:10.819
What's the matter?

35:12.154 --> 35:13.864
What?

35:14.949 --> 35:17.910
It's what you brought
me here for, isn't it?

35:19.036 --> 35:22.915
- Well, isn't it?
- I suppose so, yes.

35:22.915 --> 35:24.875
So what's your problem?

35:25.918 --> 35:28.045
Let's get on with it.

35:30.798 --> 35:34.218
You're not going to change
your fucking mind, are you?

35:35.553 --> 35:38.097
- I'm sorry.
- Let's go upstairs.

35:38.097 --> 35:41.100
OK, OK, sorry. OK?

35:48.524 --> 35:51.652
Right.

36:02.538 --> 36:04.498
This isn't the bedroom.

36:05.916 --> 36:07.877
No.

36:10.921 --> 36:13.507
So what's going on?

36:15.342 --> 36:17.761
We don't need a bed, do we?

36:19.555 --> 36:23.142
Well, no, I suppose not.

36:25.686 --> 36:28.647
- I've always preferred the floor.
- Oh?

36:29.732 --> 36:32.151
First time for everything, eh'?

36:33.235 --> 36:36.906
Why don't you... take your jacket off?

36:36.906 --> 36:40.576
Yeah, why don't I?

36:52.421 --> 36:54.507
Mm...

37:01.680 --> 37:03.766
Why don't you do the same thing?

37:04.808 --> 37:07.061
Maybe I will.

37:19.323 --> 37:22.284
You're very beautiful.

37:22.284 --> 37:26.038
- Am I?
- You know you are.

37:27.122 --> 37:30.584
Loveliest woman... I've ever seen.

37:32.086 --> 37:34.922
- Oh, Christ.
- What's wrong?

37:36.006 --> 37:39.468
Shh. One minute.

37:40.719 --> 37:44.306
Too much drink. Empty the old bladder.

37:48.143 --> 37:51.689
Did you lock this?

37:55.651 --> 37:57.736
Please! Please!

38:21.135 --> 38:23.554
Don't look at me.

39:29.453 --> 39:31.413
Jesus Christ!

39:54.228 --> 39:58.524
See? It's making me whole again.

40:01.235 --> 40:04.780
Every drop of blood you spill
puts more flesh on my bones.

40:04.780 --> 40:07.950
And we both want that, don't we?

40:10.452 --> 40:12.705
- Uh-huh.
- Good.

40:13.789 --> 40:15.666
Come here.

40:16.750 --> 40:19.211
Come here, damn you, I want to touch you.

40:22.006 --> 40:24.258
Come to Daddy.

40:36.812 --> 40:39.481
Julia?

41:01.962 --> 41:03.756
Julia?

41:07.593 --> 41:10.137
Come out, come out, wherever you are.

41:30.491 --> 41:34.078
Julia'? I was calling for you,
didn't you hear?

41:35.120 --> 41:37.456
Are you in there?

41:37.456 --> 41:40.334
You wanna cookie, little girl?

41:41.418 --> 41:44.839
- I'm feeling sick.
- Oh, babe.

41:44.839 --> 41:47.842
Is there anything I can get you?

41:47.842 --> 41:51.470
- Maybe a brandy?
- It's coming right up.

41:51.595 --> 41:54.473
I'll be down... in a minute.

41:55.766 --> 41:58.644
OK. There's no hurry.

42:22.585 --> 42:24.545
Frank?

42:30.009 --> 42:33.179
I'm hurting.

42:33.179 --> 42:36.640
- Hurting?
- My nerves are beginning to work again.

42:37.683 --> 42:40.477
- Good.
- One more, maybe two.

42:40.603 --> 42:43.772
- Not again.
- To heal me completely.

42:43.772 --> 42:47.735
Then we can be away from here
before they start to follow.

42:47.735 --> 42:50.154
- Who?
- The Cenobites.

42:50.154 --> 42:54.366
It's only a matter of time
before they find I've slipped them.

42:54.366 --> 42:57.494
- I must get away from here.
- Julia?

42:57.494 --> 42:59.538
Are you all right?

43:03.542 --> 43:05.711
Just a moment.

43:09.215 --> 43:12.218
Put on some music, will you, babe?

43:14.261 --> 43:16.847
Poor Larry, obedient as ever.

43:16.847 --> 43:19.433
Keep your voice down.

43:20.476 --> 43:23.395
Don't want "babe" to hear?

43:23.395 --> 43:25.856
You're hurting.

43:25.856 --> 43:28.150
You won't cheat me, will you?

43:28.275 --> 43:30.277
You'll stay with me, help me?

43:31.362 --> 43:34.198
Then we can be together
the way we were before.

43:34.198 --> 43:39.286
We belong to each other now...
for better, for worse.

43:41.705 --> 43:45.459
Like love... only real.

43:59.348 --> 44:02.184
I'm new here, you're going to have to wait.

44:04.520 --> 44:07.815
- Could you not do that, please?
- Where's the manager?

44:07.815 --> 44:12.194
- He's out to lunch right now.
- I want to see somebody in charge.

44:12.194 --> 44:15.614
Then you'll have to wait.

44:16.866 --> 44:19.451
- Excuse me.
- Well, excuse me!

44:23.372 --> 44:25.624
What are you doing?

44:34.717 --> 44:36.886
Give those back!

44:40.264 --> 44:42.933
Oh, my God.

44:45.686 --> 44:48.898
Get out. You get out of here.

45:09.376 --> 45:11.212
- Hi.
- Hi.

45:11.212 --> 45:14.757
Just came by to see
what you were doing after work.

45:14.882 --> 45:17.051
What's wrong?

45:17.051 --> 45:19.470
- Something weird.
- What?

45:25.684 --> 45:27.436
Nothing.

45:37.404 --> 45:40.282
Are you sure we're not
going to be interrupted?

45:42.326 --> 45:44.411
Quite sure.

45:44.411 --> 45:47.498
Only, I, er... I like to be careful.

46:50.227 --> 46:52.396
I can taste that.

46:53.564 --> 46:56.734
It's a long time since I tasted anything.

46:58.777 --> 47:01.697
You promised me an explanation.

47:04.200 --> 47:06.160
This is it.

47:06.160 --> 47:07.995
- Let me see.
- Don't touch it!

47:07.995 --> 47:11.457
It's dangerous. It opens doors.

47:12.499 --> 47:16.754
- What kind of doors?
- Doors to the pleasures of heaven or hell.

47:16.754 --> 47:18.756
I didn't care which.

47:19.882 --> 47:23.344
'I thought I'd gone to the limits.
I hadn't.

47:23.344 --> 47:27.640
'The Cenobites gave me
an experience beyond limits.

47:27.640 --> 47:30.893
'Pain and pleasure... indivisible.'

48:08.556 --> 48:10.516
They won't get me back.

48:12.977 --> 48:16.021
I'm going to live
and you're going to help me, yes?

48:16.021 --> 48:18.065
Yes.

48:18.065 --> 48:20.150
They'll never find us.

48:21.277 --> 48:24.697
Not in the whole wide world.

48:26.198 --> 48:28.659
'That punch lands home.

48:28.659 --> 48:31.412
'Boom-boom! He's got him now!
He's got him now!'

48:31.412 --> 48:35.499
'He's been knocked down again.
Referee sends him to the neutral corner.'

48:35.499 --> 48:40.171
- I thought this stuff made you sick.
- 'Moran's getting back up.'

48:40.171 --> 48:43.299
I've seen worse.

48:44.425 --> 48:48.137
- Are you all right?
- Fine.

48:49.221 --> 48:52.850
We can watch something... else if you like.
Come on!

49:04.195 --> 49:06.363
More! More!

49:07.948 --> 49:12.411
- What was that?
- I think I left a window open upstairs,

49:12.411 --> 49:14.705
- I'll go see.
- No.

49:16.123 --> 49:18.167
It was nothing.

49:19.126 --> 49:21.086
Larry!

49:21.086 --> 49:23.380
What's the matter with you anyway?

49:27.343 --> 49:30.971
It's... It's just that I hate the thunder.

49:30.971 --> 49:33.807
I'm here. You're safe.

49:35.935 --> 49:37.895
You're trembling.

49:39.605 --> 49:42.066
There's nothing to be afraid of.

49:59.124 --> 50:02.837
- I really should check it out.
- Don't go up there, please.

50:02.962 --> 50:06.590
Then... we'll both go up.

50:06.715 --> 50:09.260
- Come on.
- Larry, please.

50:09.260 --> 50:11.178
Don't worry about it, come on.

50:28.696 --> 50:30.781
- Don't.
- It's OK.

50:30.781 --> 50:32.616
It's OK.

50:44.211 --> 50:46.380
It's probably a rat.

50:47.339 --> 50:49.300
I told you.

50:49.300 --> 50:51.260
Nothing to be afraid of.

50:53.554 --> 50:55.681
Let's go downstairs. I'll make it better.

51:11.197 --> 51:13.365
No, there's just enough light.

51:17.161 --> 51:19.955
Come on, let's go.

51:37.723 --> 51:40.434
Yes, yes...

52:06.544 --> 52:08.295
No...

52:09.964 --> 52:12.508
No, please don't, no, please...

52:12.508 --> 52:14.927
I can't bear it, please.

52:14.927 --> 52:16.720
Please!

52:19.306 --> 52:21.058
Please!

52:34.071 --> 52:36.991
I can't bear it, please, no!

52:50.171 --> 52:52.339
I don't understand you.

52:53.716 --> 52:55.509
One minute...

52:56.635 --> 52:58.804
you're all over me and the next...

53:01.390 --> 53:03.726
I just don't understand you.

53:14.945 --> 53:19.700
I don't know.
Maybe we shouldn't have come back.

53:19.700 --> 53:23.120
Brooklyn certainly
wasn't any worse than this.

53:23.120 --> 53:27.666
Look - you love her
so there must be something worth loving.

53:28.375 --> 53:30.419
I wish it were that simple.

53:31.504 --> 53:33.589
I got a real problem here, kiddo.

53:34.715 --> 53:38.135
- She doesn't want to leave the house.
- Really?

53:39.178 --> 53:42.890
It's like she's... waiting for something.

53:42.890 --> 53:45.434
What?

53:45.434 --> 53:47.436
I don't know.

53:49.855 --> 53:51.607
I don't know.

53:52.691 --> 53:54.693
It's way beyond me.

53:57.321 --> 53:59.281
Look“.

54:00.407 --> 54:04.078
- Could you...? Would you...
- Uh-oh.

54:04.203 --> 54:06.413
Stop by sometime?

54:07.498 --> 54:09.875
Try to make friends?

54:09.875 --> 54:11.585
Sure.

54:11.585 --> 54:15.047
Who knows? Maybe all she needs
is somebody to talk to.

54:16.298 --> 54:19.176
- You can't love him.
- You know I don't.

54:27.643 --> 54:30.563
- So where's the harm?
- I said no.

54:30.563 --> 54:33.816
Then find me somebody else
before they come looking.

54:33.816 --> 54:36.110
Now!

55:11.478 --> 55:14.940
I, er... I get lonely sometimes.

55:18.485 --> 55:19.862
Everybody does.

55:36.504 --> 55:38.088
Come in.

55:41.800 --> 55:44.845
What is this? A game?

55:47.348 --> 55:49.558
Jesus Christ!

56:00.611 --> 56:02.196
Oh, Christ!

56:02.196 --> 56:03.739
Help me!

56:14.458 --> 56:16.210
Now get out of here!

56:16.210 --> 56:20.005
Please... don't let him kill me!

57:49.637 --> 57:52.181
Help me...

58:07.947 --> 58:11.659
- No!
- Kirsty, it's Frank.

58:11.659 --> 58:14.745
- It's Uncle Frank. You remember.
- No. No!

58:14.745 --> 58:18.457
- Come to Daddy.
- Get the fuck off of me!

58:21.335 --> 58:23.921
You've grown. You're beautiful.

58:25.339 --> 58:27.716
Don't... Don't touch me.

58:27.716 --> 58:32.972
- Don't touch me or so help me I'll...
- What'll you do?

58:34.265 --> 58:36.267
What can you do?

58:38.227 --> 58:40.771
There's nothing to be afraid of.

58:40.771 --> 58:44.567
Bet you make your daddy so proud,
don't you, beautiful?

58:44.567 --> 58:47.611
- This isn't happening!
- I used to tell myself that.

58:47.611 --> 58:52.116
I used to pretend I was dreaming
all the pain, but don't kid yourself.

58:52.116 --> 58:54.285
Some things have to be endured...

58:54.285 --> 58:57.705
and that's what makes
the pleasure so sweet!

59:09.717 --> 59:11.844
No!

59:11.844 --> 59:13.846
Give me that!

59:16.682 --> 59:18.267
- No!
- Give it to me.

59:19.351 --> 59:22.396
- You want it?
- One last time.

59:23.564 --> 59:25.357
Give me that box.

59:25.357 --> 59:27.276
- You want it?
- Give me the box!

59:27.276 --> 59:30.237
You want it? Fucking have it!

59:31.989 --> 59:34.783
No!

59:46.962 --> 59:49.548
Kirsty!

59:50.424 --> 59:53.344
'Come to Daddy?

01:00:07.858 --> 01:00:13.322
It's Frank.
You remember. It's Uncle Frank.

01:00:33.217 --> 01:00:35.177
Are you all right?

01:01:05.332 --> 01:01:07.376
You're awake?

01:01:09.837 --> 01:01:11.755
- Good girl.
- What happened?

01:01:11.755 --> 01:01:14.508
- I'll get the doctor.
- Wait, how did I get here?

01:01:14.508 --> 01:01:16.886
I won't be a moment.

01:01:20.014 --> 01:01:23.017
'Dr. Jennings...'

01:01:25.019 --> 01:01:27.104
Please, get back into bed.

01:01:27.104 --> 01:01:30.191
- I have to call my father.
- That's easily arranged,

01:01:30.316 --> 01:01:32.276
but first, back into bed.

01:01:32.276 --> 01:01:36.071
- It's important, it really...
- First things first.

01:01:36.197 --> 01:01:39.450
We'll get you a telephone
after we've talked.

01:01:40.868 --> 01:01:44.997
Does this ring any bells?
You were hanging on to it like grim death.

01:01:47.166 --> 01:01:51.337
- I don't remember.
- Well, the police will want to speak to you,

01:01:51.337 --> 01:01:54.423
- you know that?
- Oh, Christ.

01:01:55.132 --> 01:01:58.886
In the meantime,
maybe this will jog your memory.

01:02:13.859 --> 01:02:15.736
Shit.

01:06:13.265 --> 01:06:15.226
Oh, come on!

01:06:53.305 --> 01:06:57.643
The box. You opened it, we came.

01:06:57.643 --> 01:07:00.104
It's just a puzzle box.

01:07:00.104 --> 01:07:03.607
Oh no. It is a means to summon us.

01:07:03.607 --> 01:07:05.359
Who are you?

01:07:05.359 --> 01:07:09.738
Explorers in the further regions
of experience.

01:07:09.738 --> 01:07:13.284
Demons to some, angels to others.

01:07:13.284 --> 01:07:18.539
It was a mistake!
I didn't... I didn't mean to open it!

01:07:18.539 --> 01:07:20.708
It was a mistake!

01:07:21.792 --> 01:07:25.337
You can all... go to hell!

01:07:25.337 --> 01:07:29.717
- We can't. Not alone.
- You solved the box.

01:07:29.717 --> 01:07:34.847
We came. Now you must come with us,
taste our pleasures.

01:07:34.847 --> 01:07:39.935
W-Why can't you...
go away and leave me alone?

01:07:39.935 --> 01:07:42.605
Oh, no tears please.

01:07:42.605 --> 01:07:44.732
It's a waste of good suffering.

01:07:46.108 --> 01:07:49.445
Wait! Wait, wait, please wait!

01:07:49.445 --> 01:07:54.158
- No time for argument.
- You've done this before, right?

01:07:54.283 --> 01:07:57.286
Many, many times.

01:07:57.286 --> 01:08:00.456
To... To a man called Frank Cotton?

01:08:00.456 --> 01:08:02.208
Oh, yes.

01:08:02.208 --> 01:08:04.335
He escaped you.

01:08:04.335 --> 01:08:09.256
- Nobody escapes us.
- He did, I've seen him, I've seen him!

01:08:09.256 --> 01:08:12.134
- Impossible!
- He's alive!

01:08:12.134 --> 01:08:16.597
Supposing he had escaped us -
what has that to do with you?

01:08:16.597 --> 01:08:20.184
I- I can... I can lead you to him

01:08:20.184 --> 01:08:23.854
and... and you can take him
back instead of me.

01:08:23.854 --> 01:08:28.567
- Perhaps we prefer you.
- I want to hear him confess himself.

01:08:29.652 --> 01:08:33.280
Then, maybe... Maybe.

01:08:33.280 --> 01:08:36.282
But if you cheat us...

01:08:36.282 --> 01:08:40.996
We'll tear your soul apart

01:08:47.253 --> 01:08:49.129
She'll tell them everything.

01:08:49.129 --> 01:08:52.340
I don't think so,
she'll want to warn Larry first.

01:08:52.340 --> 01:08:55.094
That's probably her now.

01:08:55.094 --> 01:08:58.179
- Or the police.
- It doesn't make any difference.

01:08:59.264 --> 01:09:02.476
- Don't you care?
- What I care about is a new skin.

01:09:03.519 --> 01:09:06.438
- Maybe we should just leave.
- Like this?

01:09:06.438 --> 01:09:09.483
- Look at me.
- We can't just stay here.

01:09:11.986 --> 01:09:14.446
My brother will be home soon.

01:09:30.963 --> 01:09:32.923
What is it?

01:09:33.965 --> 01:09:36.677
I don't know where to begin.

01:09:36.802 --> 01:09:39.263
What are you talking about?

01:09:40.014 --> 01:09:41.849
It's best you see for yourself.

01:09:43.684 --> 01:09:46.519
I left her here,
I even locked the door.

01:09:46.519 --> 01:09:50.523
- Well, she's not here now.
- I'll stall looking for her.

01:09:50.523 --> 01:09:53.027
Maybe she's gone back to...

01:09:53.986 --> 01:09:55.362
To her father's house.

01:10:42.368 --> 01:10:46.121
Daddy? Daddy, it's me,
it's Kirsty, let me in!

01:10:48.123 --> 01:10:50.251
Daddy! Let me in!

01:10:59.760 --> 01:11:02.429
Kirsty? It's very late.

01:11:02.429 --> 01:11:05.182
- Where's my dad?
- What's the matter?

01:11:05.182 --> 01:11:07.518
I want to see my father!

01:11:09.395 --> 01:11:11.355
Of course.

01:11:27.496 --> 01:11:32.042
- Daddy? Daddy, you're OK. You're all right!
- Sure I am.

01:11:32.042 --> 01:11:36.046
- You're OK.
- It's OK.

01:11:36.046 --> 01:11:39.717
I was so afraid that
something happened to you.

01:11:39.717 --> 01:11:41.844
I know, I know.

01:11:44.263 --> 01:11:47.183
- I... I need to talk to you.
- Of course.

01:11:47.183 --> 01:11:50.519
It's OK, baby. Julia told me everything.

01:11:50.519 --> 01:11:53.772
Oh, no, see...

01:11:54.815 --> 01:11:57.193
Your brother Frank is upstairs -

01:11:57.318 --> 01:12:00.112
he's upstairs and he's trying to kill you,

01:12:00.237 --> 01:12:02.740
- he's gonna kill you!
- No, wait, wait.

01:12:02.740 --> 01:12:05.201
Whatever Frank did was unspeakable.

01:12:07.161 --> 01:12:09.038
Unspeakable.

01:12:11.207 --> 01:12:15.878
But believe me... it's finished with now.

01:12:15.878 --> 01:12:18.255
W-Why is it finished?

01:12:18.255 --> 01:12:20.424
He's gone.

01:12:22.676 --> 01:12:26.597
- What does "gone" mean?
- He's dead, Kirsty.

01:12:26.597 --> 01:12:32.102
He was insane, baby. A mad dog -
I had to put him out of his misery.

01:12:33.395 --> 01:12:35.898
Jesus, what a scene.

01:12:38.901 --> 01:12:43.864
When I'm feeling better, I'll go to the
police and try to make them understand.

01:12:43.864 --> 01:12:49.161
God knows, I don't really
understand myself.

01:12:52.414 --> 01:12:55.000
Did he hurt you, baby?

01:12:56.043 --> 01:12:58.087
No, I'm OK.

01:12:59.296 --> 01:13:02.466
He's better off dead. Poor Frank.

01:13:04.635 --> 01:13:07.680
I don't believe this, I don't believe this.

01:13:07.680 --> 01:13:09.723
Believe it.

01:13:12.518 --> 01:13:15.938
- You... I need to see him.
- No, you don't.

01:13:15.938 --> 01:13:17.982
Yes, I do!

01:13:19.316 --> 01:13:21.026
Yes!

01:13:23.112 --> 01:13:25.364
Show her.

01:14:26.550 --> 01:14:31.430
We want the man who did this.

01:14:31.555 --> 01:14:35.518
No. No, that wasn't the deal.

01:14:35.518 --> 01:14:37.728
He's my father and you can't have him.

01:14:37.728 --> 01:14:39.730
No!

01:14:44.443 --> 01:14:46.779
- Move!
- Kirsty.

01:14:46.779 --> 01:14:48.906
Move!

01:15:00.584 --> 01:15:03.045
- What's the matter?
- There's no time.

01:15:03.045 --> 01:15:06.882
Wait, now wait - I told you,
all that's all over with now.

01:15:06.882 --> 01:15:09.552
No, it's not. We've got to get out of here.

01:15:09.718 --> 01:15:14.223
Stay with us. We can all be happy here.

01:15:17.643 --> 01:15:20.062
No.

01:15:20.062 --> 01:15:22.773
Come to Daddy.

01:15:25.901 --> 01:15:27.862
Oh, my God.

01:15:27.862 --> 01:15:31.490
Come... to Daddy.

01:15:42.543 --> 01:15:44.628
Frank!

01:15:52.511 --> 01:15:54.430
Well...

01:15:58.100 --> 01:16:01.270
So much for the cat-and-mouse shit.

01:16:15.201 --> 01:16:17.661
No, Frank!

01:16:29.340 --> 01:16:31.800
It's nothing personal, baby.

01:16:51.153 --> 01:16:53.489
Where are you, beautiful?

01:16:58.702 --> 01:17:01.413
Come out, come out, wherever you are.

01:20:01.343 --> 01:20:03.637
Oh, my God!

01:20:03.637 --> 01:20:06.098
Daddy, Daddy...

01:20:07.141 --> 01:20:09.727
No, don't mourn him.

01:20:09.727 --> 01:20:12.646
He was dead long before
we ever touched him.

01:20:12.646 --> 01:20:15.482
- Bastard!
- Hush, now.

01:20:16.567 --> 01:20:19.278
Everything's all right.

01:20:19.403 --> 01:20:21.488
- Frank's here.
- Bastard!

01:20:21.488 --> 01:20:24.366
Your dear old Uncle Frank.

01:20:31.123 --> 01:20:33.667
What the hell is that?

01:21:24.844 --> 01:21:28.305
- Frank.
- No!

01:21:29.682 --> 01:21:31.767
We had to hear it from your own lips.

01:21:32.977 --> 01:21:35.563
This isn't for your eyes.

01:21:36.605 --> 01:21:39.692
You set me up, bitch!

01:22:45.382 --> 01:22:48.969
Jesus wept.

01:23:12.326 --> 01:23:14.870
Not leaving us so soon, are you?

01:23:54.577 --> 01:23:58.122
We have such sights to show you.

01:24:02.918 --> 01:24:05.254
Oh, shit!

01:24:08.883 --> 01:24:11.719
No, don't do that.

01:24:11.719 --> 01:24:14.847
Go to hell!

01:24:44.210 --> 01:24:46.420
Kirsty?

01:24:46.962 --> 01:24:49.423
Kirsty?

01:25:13.447 --> 01:25:15.032
No...

01:25:35.511 --> 01:25:37.304
Steve!

01:25:39.473 --> 01:25:41.433
No!

01:25:48.649 --> 01:25:51.819
Oh, Kirsty. Thank God you're OK.

01:25:52.778 --> 01:25:54.738
Let's get the hell out of here - now!

01:25:57.741 --> 01:26:00.786
Oh, no... Oh, God! No!

01:26:00.786 --> 01:26:03.163
- What next? Open!
- Steve!

01:30:06.991 --> 01:30:09.827
What's your pleasure, sir?
